messages:
Ava Martinez: FYI I got a bug report: the quickstart README TS snippet uses a default import which fails in ESM-first projects (no esModuleInterop). Users see `TypeError: Redwood is not a constructor`.

Ethan Lee: Oof. Which lines?

Ava Martinez: Current:```ts
import Redwood from 'redwood-inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
```

Maya Chen: We export a named factory. Fix to show named import + both CJS/ESM JS variants so copy/paste works:
```ts
// ESM / TS
import { createClient } from 'redwood-inference';
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });

// CommonJS
const { createClient } = require('redwood-inference');
const client = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
```

Ethan Lee: Can you add a one-line troubleshooting note about tsconfig `esModuleInterop`? Newcomers keep toggling flags and it confuses them.

Maya Chen: Yep. I'll open a docs PR with README change, a short FAQ entry, and a tiny smoke CI step (npm pack + run a minimal TS ESM project) to prevent regressions.

doc-bot: Issue created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/issues/579 

Ava Martinez: Thanks! Adding a note to the internal onboarding checklist for demos so SEs don't hit this live.

Maya Chen: PR opened and CI started.
